ENVIRONMENT NOTE (pre-existing, out-of-scope — NOT introduced by this artifact)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The TeslaSync app target does NOT build at HEAD. A clean baseline build BEFORE any
of this artifact's files existed already fails (22+ failures). Root causes are
pre-existing duplicate-symbol definitions and Swift-6.3 strictness in unrelated
files, NONE under Features/Telemetry:
  • StatusApiDocsPage.swift (Features/System) redefines enum TSSpacing + TSRadius,
    duplicating apps/design/generated/apple/Tokens.swift → module-wide
    "ambiguous use of 'xs'/'md'/'lg'/'x2xl'/…'" cascade.
  • TirePressureUnit defined twice (Features/VehicleSystems/TirePressureModels.swift
    AND dashboard-widgets/TirePressureHistoryWidget.Projection.swift) — conflicting.
  • HeroStatus defined twice (shared-surfaces/StatusHero.Adapter.swift AND
    Features/System/SystemStatusModels.swift) — conflicting.
  • Swift-6.3 "cannot use explicit 'return' in ViewBuilder" in pre-existing
    *.Previews.swift (ScheduledExportsPanel, SafetyHistoryWidget).
This is the same condition the sibling page:telemetry/SignalsWorkspace ledger row
documents ("~698 ambiguous-symbol errors across design-system/generated files
(none in Features/Telemetry)"). It blocks the full xcodebuild + the project-wide
swiftlint --strict regardless of this artifact.

VERIFICATION STRATEGY
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Because the broken baseline aborts before the SignalExplorer batch is even
scheduled, this artifact's seven page files were verified by an isolated
swiftc -typecheck against the REAL design tokens (apps/design/generated/apple/
Tokens.swift), the REAL shared value types (SignalsWorkspaceTypes.swift), and
